class:: Voicing
summary:: Binary and continuous voiced/harmonic evidence
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Estimates whether a frame contains stable voiced or harmonic excitation without requiring the caller to use its F0. code::\periodicity:: returns NSDF peak evidence directly. code::\hybrid:: combines that evidence with a silence gate and a zero-crossing plausibility factor. Version 0.1 is a deterministic model-free descriptor, not a trained speech classifier or a calibrated probability.

The first output applies code::threshold:: to the continuous second output. Silence returns two zeros. It is practically similar to link::Classes/Pitch::'s code::hasFreq:: output, but supplies continuous evidence independently from the final pitch decision.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: frameSize
Literal power-of-two frame size from 256 through 8192.

argument:: hop
Update hop as a frame fraction from 0.0625 through 1.

argument:: minFreq
Minimum periodic frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Maximum periodic frequency and zero-crossing reference in Hz.

argument:: method
Literal code::\periodicity:: or code::\hybrid::.

argument:: threshold
Decision threshold from 0 through 1 for the binary output.

returns::
An Array: binary voiced flag and continuous evidence from 0 through 1.

method:: latency
Returns approximate first-result latency in seconds.

instancemethods::

examples::
Voicing separates periodic, harmonic vocal or instrumental sustains from noisy consonants, transient bursts, and breath. In this example, it drives a dual-path adaptive processor: voiced sections route through a lush stereo chorus resonator, while unvoiced sibilance and breath route into a gritty, saturated distortion stage. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: plots the continuous voicing evidence in real time.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var voicing = Voicing.kr(source, 1024, 0.25, 80, 1200, \hybrid, 0.5);
        var voicedFlag = voicing[0];
        var evidence = voicing[1];
        var voicedSmooth = evidence.lag(0.04);

        // Voiced path: stereo chorus resonator
        var voicedSig = source * voicedSmooth;
        var chorus = CombC.ar(voicedSig, 0.05, 0.02 + SinOsc.kr(0.4, [0, pi/2], 0.003), 0.4);

        // Unvoiced path: driven saturation for breath/consonants
        var unvoicedSig = source * (1.0 - voicedSmooth);
        var driven = (unvoicedSig * 6).tanh * 0.25 ! 2;

        var sound = (source * 0.2 ! 2) + chorus + driven;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, evidence) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Voicing Probability", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

